      "time_allocation": "45h (60 sessions) contact hours + 1h final exam + 104h self-study",
      "pre_requisite": "CSD203, AIL303m",
      "description": "This speech processing course comprehensively explains how humans and machines generate, transmit, and process speech signals. The course covers speech production, phonetics, acoustic analysis, speech perception, speech recognition, natural language processing, and speech synthesis. Students will learn about the principles and algorithms behind various speech-processing techniques, including signal processing, machine learning, and deep learning. The course also covers speech processing applications in speech recognition, speech recognition, speech synthesis, and speech enhancement. Upon completing the course, students will have a solid foundation in speech processing and be equipped with the necessary skills to tackle real-world speech-processing problems.",
      "studenttasks": "'- Students must attend at least 80% of contact slots in order to be accepted to the final examination.\n- Student is responsible to do all exercises, assignments and labs given by instructor in class or at home and submit on time\n- Use laptop in class only for learning purpose\n- Promptly access to the FU FLM at http://flm.fpt.edu.vn for up-to-date course information",
      "tools": "No",
      "scoring_scale": "10",
      "decisionno_mm_dd_yyyy": "1318/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 11/27/2025",
      "isapproved": "True",
      "note": "1) On-going Assessment\n- 2 Assignments: 30%\n- 2 progress tests: 30%\n2) 1 Final Exam: 40%\n3) Final Result 100% (The Final result - including bonus score - is not greater than 10)\nCompletion Criteria:\n1) Every on-going assessment component > 0\n2) Final Exam Score >= 4 & Final Result >= 5\nBonus score for accepted paper (email accepted/ published):\nISI/Scopus Q1, Q2: 5\nISI/Scopus Q3, Q4: 3\nScopus Q1, Q2: 3\nScopus Q3, Q4: 2\nSource to check Scopus ranking: https://www.scimagojr.com/\nSource to check ISI: https://mjl.clarivate.com",
